\ results/drafts/numfirst-722.4 - the gene numfirst's prototype (Iteration 722; results/drafts/esolangs-717.md):
\ a token of the form [0-9]+ is converted before the lookup, while BASE is at least 10 (so it always converts) and no
\ name of that form is defined. Loaded last among a design's overlays by results/drafts/numfirst-722.py: INTERPRET8's
\ body becomes INTERPRET's (tools/layout.py's X8 swap). The rest of INTERPRET is the kernel's, step for step.
\ Not built: the header word setting NUMNAMES when a program defines such a name (a test per definition, not per
\ token - none of the workloads defines one, and the outputs are compared); a leading '-' takes the old path.

VARIABLE NUMNAMES  0 NUMNAMES !

: DIGITS? ( c-addr u --- f )
  DUP 0= IF 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
  OVER + SWAP DO I C@ 48 - 10 U< 0= IF UNLOOP 0 EXIT THEN LOOP -1 ;

: NUMFIRST? ( c-addr --- f )
\ The first character a digit already (INTERPRET8's test): the rest, BASE, the flag.
  COUNT DIGITS? BASE @ 10 < 0= AND NUMNAMES @ 0= AND ;

: INTERPRET8 ( ---)
  BEGIN
   32 WORD DUP C@
  WHILE
   DUP 1+ C@ 48 - 10 U< IF DUP NUMFIRST? ELSE 0 THEN
   IF
    NUMBER? DROP DROP STATE @ IF POSTPONE LITERAL ELSE ?STACK THEN
   ELSE
    FIND DUP
    IF
     -1 = STATE @ AND
     IF
      COMPILE,
     ELSE
      EXECUTE ?STACK
     THEN
    ELSE DROP
     NUMBER? DUP 0= HANDLER @ AND IF -13 THROW THEN 0= ABORT" Undefined word"
     DPL @ 0< IF DROP STATE @ IF POSTPONE LITERAL ELSE ?STACK THEN
     ELSE STATE @ IF SWAP POSTPONE LITERAL POSTPONE LITERAL ELSE ?STACK THEN THEN
    THEN
   THEN
  REPEAT   DROP
;
